# Used by `docker compose up` (env_file for the `web` service). For local
# (non-Docker) development, copy web/.env.example into web/.env instead —
# see web/README.md.
#
# There is nothing to set here: `docker-compose.yml` passes DATABASE_URL to
# the container directly, and every other credential (admin password,
# OpenAI, GitHub, Spotify/X/Google, SMTP, branding, Alexandria, the JSON API
# token) is configured exclusively through the web interface — the
# first-run /setup wizard, then /admin/settings and /admin/account. This
# file is kept as the `env_file` target `docker-compose.yml` expects; it can
# stay empty.
